  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 146 PM CST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nThe long term forecast remains generally quiet. An upper level \ntrough is forecast to emerge out of the Desert Southwest and \nnorthern Mexico over the weekend. PoPs remain low (less than 30%),\nhowever, during this time period, with the higher rain chances in\nthe Permian Basin and Edwards Plateau. Otherwise, highs Friday \nthrough Sunday will mainly be in the upper 50s and 60s. An upper \nlevel ridge looks to build into the region early next week which \nwould bring a return of mild temperatures and dry conditions.",
